ting arm can see it, and what the deletion leaves green. The generator,\n36\t   stale/fresh/extra, collision, prune, honesty-sentence and work-branch\n37\t   assertions are untouched in both the cell and the fixture.\n38\t3. `LLR-208.detail` NAMES the wiring: the `verdict-rollup` regen row, its\n39\t   `docs/reviews/` arming guard and printed skip, its LEAF position in the\n40\t   dependency order, and that membership in the trunk regen set is part of the\n41\t   contract rather than an implementation accident — because it is the only\n42\t   thing making the exclusive-writer clause above it true. Both cells therefore\n43\t   carry a real content edit, so the delta-driven mint presents both rows and\n44\t   `LLR-208` does not strand without a queued approver.\n45\t\n46\tHarness: smoke `1523 passed, 8 skipped`, budget `34.6s vs 60s -> within`; full\n47\tunfiltered suite driven before close (result in `docs/log.d/`).\n48\t\n49\t## Context\n50\t\n51\tDrafted by WI-586 (its ## Dispositions section) and minted at its merge - drafts-not-mints, ruling R1/R3.\n52\t\n53\tVERDICT THIS CONTINUES:\n54\t`docs/reviews/wi-586-adjudicate-llr-207-llr-208/009-ADJUDICATE-082b9e1.md`,\n55\tgoverning line `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=4`. The first adjudication found `LLR-208`\n56\tand `TC-206` ready on their text; three independent rereads since have found the\n57\tsame downward coverage gap, and this one re-drove it rather than inheriting it.\n58\t\n59\tIN SCOPE — the missing detector and the TWO registry cells it corrects.\n60\t`LLR-208.detail` states the rollup is \"regenerated by the trunk step\" and\n61\t`TC-206.expected` repeats that \"the serial merge step runs\" the regenerator —\n62\tthe clause that makes SR-170's exclusive-writer contract true for this artifact.\n63\tIts four cited tests drive the generator itself, the generated artifact's\n64\tfreshness-enforcer declaration, the enforcer's commit-floor wiring, and the\n65\twork-branch stand-down set. None asserts that `trunk_step.RE