{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CejJZbb3w7F3MTi4PDQps","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mfq3Edt3VRjUs6jqLuFdT2","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/venv-symlink-trap-2026-09-02.md","old_string":"**Running a lane worktree WITHOUT making a `.venv` (confirmed WI-574,\n2026-09-02):** worktrees under `/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/<branch>/`\nhave no `.venv` and must not grow one — just invoke the trunk interpreter by\nabsolute path from the worktree root:\n`/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n auto`.\nEverything (pytest, xdist, the kit scripts) resolves fine against the worktree's\nown cwd. Caveat to expect and record honestly: the commit hook runs under\nambient `/usr/local/bin/python3`, which has no ruff, so every commit prints the\n\"A DECLARED CHECK DID NOT RUN — format\" banner. Harmless for a docs-only lane;\na lane touching Python must run `ruff format` through the trunk interpreter\nitself before committing.","new_string":"**Running a lane worktree (worktrees under\n`/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/<branch>/` ship with NO `.venv`).**\nTwo routes; the hazard this memory names is the SYMLINK, not a venv as such.\n\n- *Borrow the trunk interpreter* (WI-574, 2026-09-02): invoke it by absolute\n  path from the worktree root,\n  `/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n auto`.\n  Everything resolves against the worktree's own cwd. **Cost:** the commit hook\n  still runs under ambient `/usr/local/bin/python3`, which has no ruff, so every\n  commit prints the \"A DECLARED CHECK DID NOT RUN — format\" banner and the\n  `format` step is NOT grading the commit.\n- *Build a REAL venv in the lane* (confirmed WI-592, 2026-09-04):\n  `python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -r requirements-dev.txt`\n  (~1 min). `.venv` is gitignored, so the tree stays clean. This is what makes\n  the hook find ruff — the very next commit ran `format ... 234 files already\n  formatted  PASS` instead of the skip banner. Prefer this on any lane that\n  touches Python.\n\n**Never a symlink, either way**, and remove a lane's real `.venv` before\nunloading so the unload GC never walks it."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1604,"cache_read_input_tokens":102955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1604},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3268e15-f5cc-41f6-82dc-5bdc2fb680b2","uuid":"6ddc422f-c3f5-48c5-aca1-b160edcb6074","request_id":"req_011CejJZajhUE1WiPNcXdsrt"}
