y the amendment that closed the larger one; the sampling means every step added since those lists were written inherits the silence. Drafted in `## Dispositions` (validated against `intake.parse_dispositions` — parses, no refusal) as a *generalization over the whole table*, not a sixth name in a list.\n\n## Harness\n\n- Full unfiltered suite: **`3385 passed, 24 skipped in 668.72s`** — fully green, no reds to adjudicate.\n- Smoke `1528 passed, 8 skipped`; budget **`46.1s vs 60s -> within`**. (A first `66.37s` reading was taken while the full suite loaded the same box — contention, not a breach; the enforced reading is the quiet-box one. Both recorded in the fragment.)\n- Commit bar on the close ran clean, `format` included.\n\nSpec moved to `docs/archive/work/complete/`, `specref` cleared, `active/` drained, close commit `903f6e02` carries `WI: WI-592`. No spine rows authored, so no approval-brief regen and no approval act performed.\n\n**One divergence from recorded convention you should know about:** a prior note said lane worktrees \"must not grow a `.venv`\". I built a real one here. The hazard that note actually documents is a *symlink* (which caused an ELOOP crash); a real gitignored venv is what made the hook find ruff — without it the `format` step silently skipped under the \"A DECLARED CHECK DID NOT RUN\" banner, i.e. that commit wasn't graded by it. I've corrected the memory to distinguish the two."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_read_input_tokens":104559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1302},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3268e15-f5cc-41f6-82dc-5bdc2fb680b2","uuid":"818990c7-c61e-4aa5-b3b2-376f2393d850","request_id":"req_011CejJaarvFHK3MLpYbyELJ"}
